@startuml fig_cache_stale_fill
!include _style.puml
' Book figure — the stale-fill race and its source-generation fence.
' Form: sequence. Evidence status: observed result — it illustrates registered claim
' v2-15 (three shared instances under relaxed freshness) by showing the mechanism its
' wrong reads came from. Scope: the stale-fill race only; the strict-after-acknowledgement
' contract and its acknowledgement boundary are a separate figure. The figure embeds no
' rate of its own; the rate is stated in the claim card beside it.
title the stale-fill race, and source-generation validation

actor "reader R1" as R
actor "reader R2\n(another instance)" as R2
participant "writer W" as W
database "source\n(database)" as DB
participant "shared cache" as C

group unsafe: "publish after commit" is not enough
  R -> DB : 1 read  → S0 / v0
  DB --> R : committed S0 (version v0)
  W -> DB : 2 write S1 · commit
  W -> DB : 3 source version := v1
  W -> C : 4 invalidate key
  R -> C : 5 publish S0 (fill)
  R2 -> C : 6 read → hits the stale fill S0
  note right of C
    A committed-but-older value is now resident.
    This is the race the claim's wrong reads came from:
    the invalidation at step 4 orders nothing about
    the fill already in flight at step 5.
  end note
end

group fenced: source-generation validation refuses the fill
  R -> DB : 1 current source generation?
  DB --> R : 2 v1
  note over R : R1 observed v0. v1 <> v0, so R1 must not publish S0.
  R -> C : 3 publish nothing
  R2 -> C : 4 read → miss
  R2 -> DB : 5 authoritative read
  DB --> R2 : S1 / v1
  R2 -> C : 6 fill S1 / v1 (safe)
  note over R2, C : R2 served the source, not a stale copy.
end
@enduml
